--- step 1: STRIDE on the upload flow (worked case, authored) ---
Flow: user -> upload endpoint -> virus-scan stub -> file store -> manager preview
T1 (Tampering): malicious PDF exploits the scanner stub -> mitigate: stub runs sandboxed, files quarantined until verdict; verify by submitting EICAR-style benign test file.
T2 (Information disclosure): preview renders PDF with embedded JS -> mitigate: preview serves sanitized raster, never the raw file; verify by uploading a JS-carrying PDF and inspecting the preview response.
(threat list authored; no CLI by design for this step)

