--- step 4: diff review (worked case) ---
REVIEW FINDINGS (written as for the developer):
  1. auth.py (request_reset): reset token in URL query string - tokens land in server logs, browser history, referers. Fix: deliver via POST body link carrying a one-time path token, or keep the token out of logged URLs.
  2. auth.py (request_reset/do_reset): no rate limit on reset requests - user enumeration + email bombing. Fix: per-IP/per-account throttling with backoff.
  3. auth.py (do_reset): token never expires and is not consumed on use - replayable indefinitely. Fix: 15-minute expiry, single-use delete on success.
  4. auth.py: token_hex(8) = 64 bits; acceptable, but state the entropy budget in a comment so the next reader doesn't 'optimize' it down.

